# census-exclusions.manifest — TRACKED `test-*.sh` files that NO selection root
# walks ON PURPOSE (your-org/nexus-code#1620).
#
# Read by:   monitor/watcher/run-tests.sh (`_rt_census`) on every root-walking run.
# Enforced:  bash monitor/watcher/test-run-tests-shape-census.sh (§B3).
#
# The runner's census names every tracked `test-*.sh` no root in
# `_RT_SUITE_ROOTS` walks and reddens the run, because a suite nothing selects
# appears ZERO times in any band log. Some such files are not suites: a fixture
# or stub that a suite EXECUTES may need a `test-*.sh` name. Declare each one
# here — ONE PATH PER ROW, never a directory or a pattern, because a structural
# rule ("everything under fixtures/") would admit a real suite misplaced there
# without a line anywhere saying so, which is the invisible exclusion #1078 and
# #1620 are about.
#
# FORMAT:  <repo-relative path>|<reason>
#   The reason is REQUIRED (why the file is never run, and which suite uses it).
#   Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored.
#
# EVERY ROW IS RE-CHECKED ON EVERY CENSUS, and each of these is RED:
#   - no `|`, an empty path, an empty reason, or a path already listed (REFUSED);
#   - a path that is not a tracked `test-*.sh`, or one a root already walks
#     (STALE — delete the row in the PR that moved or removed the file);
#   - this file present but untracked (its rows would not exist on CI).
# Every applied exclusion is printed as `EXCLUDED: <path> — <reason>` under the
# census line, which carries `excluded=N`, on every run, green or red.
#
# Empty at creation (2026-09-22): no tracked `test-*.sh` lives outside a root.
